ause uh we know  broadly uh that uh the russians uh are  want to point to a fabricated pretext uh  before undertaking aggression uh it's  precisely what they did uh in 2014 in  ukraine uh these claims of genocide have  haunting echoes of what we heard in 2014  regarding the persecution of russian  speakers in eastern ukraine and crimea  this is  in some ways eerily similar  to  what we have experienced before and so  now that we hear vladimir putin we hear  other russian officials uh pointing to  genocide  uh  pointing to  uh  the  uh  pointing to what you know we have heard  uh in the past uh it gives us great  concern that this could be part  of the same playbook that they are  reprising uh in the context of 2022.  thank you yes  brazilian presidential equals another  match while doing coaching in moscow  bosom did not mention the ukrainian  crisis but he said that he has  solidarity with russia  how do you say his declarations his trip  and the approximation between brazil and  russia at this moment  and if this could affect the relations  between brazil and the united states in  the future  well we know that any number of  countries and in fact the international  community  is broadly and deeply concerned  about what we are all seeing uh taking  place  with russia and ukraine at this very  moment  as  democratic countries  as democratic leaders in our in our  hemisphere uh we in brazil uh we feel  that  uh we have a responsibility to stand up  uh for the values that we  uh and at  the heart of those values  are the principles of uh the rules-based  international order uh these are this is  the order that has uh over the course of  more than seven decades now uh has  fueled unprecedented levels of  prosperity security and stability uh in  europe in the indo-pacific but also uh  in our own uh hemisphere and so that's  why it is our hope that uh president  bolsonaro uh will have uh taken  advantage of this opportunity uh this  meeting with president putin uh to  re